  {
    "name": "get_environment",
    "title": "Get weather, air quality and pollen",
    "description": "Fetch the weather, air quality, pollen and UV the user's stored days had (environment module): per day the temperature (min, max, mean, feels-like high), precipitation, sunshine hours, pressure and humidity, and while air quality is on, PM2.5 (mean and peak), PM10, NO2, the ozone 8-hour high, the European AQI peak, UV, dust and six pollen kinds; plus coverage and a summary (hot nights, very poor air days, high pollen days). These are modelled outdoor conditions at a coarse location (ERA5 and CAMS, 9 to 45 km grid), not the user's personal exposure; describe co-occurrence, never a cause. Null means not covered, never zero. Carries no coordinates and no place names. Each result lists the attributions to show with it (Open-Meteo, CC BY 4.0; Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service). Returns { present: false, reason: \"module_disabled\" } when the environment module is off, and no_data / outside_window when nothing is stored in the window.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "window": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "last7days",
            "last30days",
            "last90days",
            "lastYear",
            "allTime"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "outputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
